cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive or its series, please cite it and the article it accompanies."
type: software
title: "Same-path controls for keystroke detectors: conditions, code, records, series and history"
abstract: >-
  The conditions, code, records, released series and git history of an evaluation procedure for detectors that tell
  human from machine typing by keystroke timing: two paired controls on the detector's path, a replay of human records
  through the machine's path and each machine session's plan against its recording, on one Windows machine with a hook
  and a browser page (Chrome and Firefox). Runs v7 to v7v; every computation ran a script on conditions committed
  before its values. The released series hold the kinds and times of the planned and recorded key presses, without
  keys, text or person identifiers. The code is under the MIT License; the documents and conditions under CC BY 4.0;
  the records keep the terms of the keystroke data they count; the series made from KUPA-KEYS are under
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and the others under CC BY 4.0 (REUSE.toml, LICENSES/, LICENSE-docs).
